.TH PIS 1 "15 November 2026" "pis 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pis \- Slackware post-installation configuration assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pis
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PIS
is a dialog-based collection of Bash scripts for selected Slackware 15.0 and current
post-installation tasks. It configures locale, keyboard, date/time, optional
NTP synchronization, login, users, wheel administration, X sessions,
ELILO/LILO/GRUB kernels and selected package managers
on x86 and x86_64.
.PP
Before replacing a configuration file, PIS creates a private backup under
.IR /var/log/PIS/backups .
PIS can display and restore these backups.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Show the installed version.
.TP
.BR -c , " --check"
Display the system and compatibility check.
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " FILE
Export settings recorded by PIS to a versioned profile. Passwords are not
exported.
.TP
.BR -f , " --file " FILE
Validate, preview and apply a PIS profile.
.TP
.B --restore
Select and restore an automatic PIS backup.
.SH PROFILES
PIS 0.3 and 0.4 profiles use
.B PIS_PROFILE_VERSION=1
and store portable values such as the full slackpkg mirror URL. Unknown
settings, incompatible repositories and invalid values are rejected before
changes are made. A password is requested interactively when a missing user
must be created.
.PP
PIS 0.2 profiles are rejected because they may contain plaintext passwords.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/PIS
Private state recorded by PIS.
.TP
.I /var/log/PIS/backups
Automatic backups and their index.
.TP
.I /etc/localtime
Timezone data selected by Slackware timeconfig.
.TP
.I /etc/hardwareclock
Hardware-clock mode selected by Slackware timeconfig.
.TP
.I /etc/ntp.conf
NTP configuration. PIS manages only its delimited NTP block.
.TP
.I /etc/rc.d/rc.ntpd
Native Slackware NTP startup script; its executable mode enables startup.
.TP
.I /boot/efi/EFI/Slackware/elilo.conf
ELILO configuration, when the kernel module is used.
.TP
.I /etc/lilo.conf
LILO configuration, when detected.
.TP
.I /boot/grub/grub.cfg
GRUB configuration, when detected.
.TP
.I /etc/grub.d/09_pis
Explicit PIS-managed GRUB entries. The selected default kernel is emitted first;
automatic GRUB entries remain available as fallbacks.
.PP
For 32-bit LILO installations, the kernel menu offers a legacy-BIOS mode that
creates compact initrds and validates low-memory placement before installing
the boot map.
.SH NOTES
When multiple bootloader configurations are present, PIS requires an explicit
selection. The GRUB package alone is not considered a configured bootloader;
/boot/grub/grub.cfg must exist.
.PP
PIS uses existing Slackware configuration files and does not replace the
distribution's network and service configuration utilities.
.PP
The Date and Time menu invokes Slackware timeconfig and can configure the
global NTP pool, enable or disable rc.ntpd, and display the recorded state.
